    {
      "id": "input.requestId",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Request ID",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "What ties a reply to what it replies to. A manager keeps many of these in flight on one socket and has nothing else to tell the answers apart by."
    },
    {
      "id": "requestId",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Request ID",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "via": "minint",
      "about": [
        "RFC 3416 §4.1's Integer32, and the reason every value here goes through `minint`.",
        "",
        "821915 is three octets — 0c 8a 9b — because X.690 §8.3.2 forbids a leading octet that could be",
        "dropped, and 0x0c has its top bit clear so nothing needs to precede it. The same rule pads: an",
        "unsigned 9740722 is 00 94 a1 b2, four octets for a three-octet number, because 0x94 would read",
        "as negative. So the width is a function of the value in both directions and no declared width",
        "is right for both."
      ]
    },
