    {
      "id": "input.varbinds",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Varbinds",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": {
        "oid": "Text",
        "tag": "Int",
        "value": "Bytes"
      },
      "purpose": "What is being asked about, one record per binding. The name is dotted — '1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0' — because an OID arc cannot contain a dot, unlike a DNS label, so the string loses nothing.",
      "about": "The value is octets and a tag, not a typed thing. A GetRequest sends NULL (tag 5, no octets) for every one of them, and what comes back is whatever the MIB says that object is."
    },
    {
      "id": "varbind",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "one binding",
      "about": [
        "RFC 3416 §4.1's VarBind: a name and a value, in a SEQUENCE of their own.",
        "",
        "How many there are is on the wire nowhere. The list has a length in octets and no count, and one",
        "varbind is followed by another that looks exactly like it — so the reading counts octets against",
        "that length and stops when it has spent them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "varbindTag",
      "kind": "field",
