    {
      "id": "oid",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the object name",
      "about": [
        "X.690 §8.19. A run of arcs, each a base-128 group chain — the same shape MIDI, protobuf and",
        "DWARF use, and the reason the form carrying it is named after the notion rather than after BER.",
        "",
        "Two nodes rather than one repetition, because §8.19.4 merges the first two arcs into a single",
        "subidentifier: 1.3 is 40*1+3 = 43 = 0x2b. So the first one is not one of the run — it is a",
        "different number computed from two of the caller's — exactly as a DNS name's root is not one of",
        "its labels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "oidFirst",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "the first subidentifier",
      "form": {
        "of": "varint",
        "order": "MostSignificantFirst",
        "max": 5
      },
      "about": "X.690 §8.19.4: 40 times the first arc plus the second. Which is why the octets have one fewer element than the name does, and why 0x2b is the beginning of very nearly every OID anyone has ever seen — 1.3 is iso.org."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.oidFirst",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the first two arcs, merged",
      "runs": "40 * undecimal(index(split(item.oid, '.'), 0)) + undecimal(index(split(item.oid, '.'), 1))",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "arcs",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the rest of the name",
      "about": "One field per arc after the merged pair. A run inside a run — the arcs of THIS binding — so what it is written once per item of is taken off the binding being written rather than handed in beside the list."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.itsArcs",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the arcs after the first two",
      "runs": "split(index(suffixes(item.oid, '.'), 2), '.')",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": "Text",
      "about": "`suffixes` gives every tail of a dotted name, so index 2 is the name with its first two arcs gone. Built for DNS suffix sharing and it is the same question here."
    },
    {
      "id": "arc",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "an arc",
      "form": {
        "of": "varint",
        "order": "MostSignificantFirst",
        "max": 5
      },
      "about": "Seven bits per octet, top bit set on all but the last. 2021 is 8f 65 and 10 is 0a, and the reading tells them apart from the octets alone — which is why nothing has to say how wide an arc is."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.arc",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this arc",
      "runs": "undecimal(item)",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "valueTag",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "the value tag",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 8
      },
      "about": "What kind of thing came back, and the one field here whose meaning is outside the message format: 0x05 is NULL, 0x04 an OCTET STRING, 0x43 TimeTicks. Which of them is right for a given name is in a MIB, not on the wire."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.valueTag",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "what kind of value this is",
      "runs": "item.tag",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "valid.valueTag",
